v 3
d hlmr2: Nakagawa marginal and conditional R-squared after mixed
d
d hlmr2 computes the Nakagawa and Schielzeth (2013) marginal and
d conditional R-squared for linear multilevel models fit by mixed.
d The marginal R-squared is the share of outcome variance explained
d by the fixed effects; the conditional R-squared adds the random
d effects.  Results are stored in r() for use in loops and tables.
d Works with one or more nested random-effects levels and with both
d the sd() and var() parameter labels that estat sd produces across
d Stata versions.
d
d Requires: Stata 16 or newer
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
d
f hlmr2.ado
f hlmr2.sthlp
